WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:14.450
Looking backwards, I think that the curb appeal
of the great quadrangle lent a prestige to

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:22.470
the institution that made it great before
it was great.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:28.840
It was a really smart move and the architecture
was well worked-out, and the great lawn was

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.160
a marvelous idea.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.210
We used to drive in to the symphony and we
would drive down [Memorial] Drive, coming

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:42.680
from Fitchburg on route 2, then down the drive.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:58.910
And we would have a lunch at a Howard Johnson's
that was up where the hotel is now, and we

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.480
went past MIT on our way to Longfellow Bridge.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:13.630
And I knew the school and I liked science
in high school and I guess, that way, I just

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.479
didn't think of any other school that was
my choice.

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:23.740
MIT was very remote for people that lived
in Cambridge, even though we lived almost

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.990
on top of it.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.450
We had nothing in common with them.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.830
I don't even think, when we were living in
Newtowne Court that they had dormitories at

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.310
that point.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:41.970
Talking about MIT, honestly, I never knew
that they moved to Cambridge.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:49.479
I always thought they was here and started
here.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:55.590
Of course, they've been here longer than I
have, so that's why I thought it was always

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.520
originally here.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:05.250
The uniqueness of it being on the river makes
it almost something you can't miss, because

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.590
the Charles River and the Boston skyline is
unbelievable.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:20.500
But even in the beginning, MIT was just so
popularly known that you always marveled at

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.590
it.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.890
You'd drive by Mass.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:30.760
Ave. and you'd see the big columns and the
stairs, and you go "wow," and you'd think

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.730
Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:42.599
Technology -- it was something great.When
I grew up we'd just got TV.

00:02:42.599 --> 00:02:46.349
You had to wait for the TV to heat up.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:56.140
So technology was what you saw happening,
and you knew technology was MIT and that they

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.100
were part of it.

